    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκαθεύδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sleep away from home,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὸ ἱερόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.4.1
				</span></i>
			; of a woman separated from her husband, <i>sleep apart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				399
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fall asleep over</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1.13d
			</span></i>.</div>
